course: dictionary
lesson: 11287
title: Wrongdoing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wrongdoing is a noun. It means bad or illegal behaviour, or doing something wrong. It is a formal word, so you will often meet it in news reports and official writing. «The company denied any wrongdoing.» The company said it had not done anything wrong.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Denied tells you the company said no, and any wrongdoing is the thing it said it did not do. So wrongdoing must mean bad behaviour. Try the swap test: put "doing something wrong" in place of wrongdoing, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Wrongdoing is usually uncountable, so you say "wrongdoing" when you mean bad behaviour in general. You can also say "a wrongdoing" for one bad act. Useful phrases are deny any wrongdoing, accused of wrongdoing and admit wrongdoing.
fact: Wrongdoing means bad or illegal behaviour, or doing something wrong.
fact: «Accused of wrongdoing» means someone is said to have done something wrong.
fact: «Admit wrongdoing» means to say honestly that you did something wrong.
fact: «Irregularities» in official reports can mean fraud, which is cheating people out of money, or other wrongdoing.
fact: Loyalty means standing by your friends, family and groups, but loyalty to wrongdoing is not a virtue.
exercise: «The company denied any wrongdoing.» What does wrongdoing mean? | A large building | Doing something kind for others | A new idea | *Doing something wrong
exercise: Which phrase means to say honestly that you did something wrong? | Praise for helping others | *Admit wrongdoing | Deny any wrongdoing | Invent a new game
exercise: «Irregularities» in official reports can mean what? | Birthday parties | *Fraud, or other wrongdoing | Long summer holidays
test: Which phrase means the same as "said to have done something wrong"? | *Accused of wrongdoing, said to have broken the rules | Accused of wrongdoing | Praised for kindness | Excused from lessons
test: Loyalty to wrongdoing is not a good thing. What does this teach a child? | Wrongdoing is a kind of game | *A real friend never asks you to lie for them | Loyalty means doing whatever a friend says | A friend should always keep secrets, even harmful ones
exam: «A promise to hide wrongdoing does not bind you.» What does this mean? | Wrongdoing is a promise | *You do not have to keep a promise to hide wrongdoing | Promises always have to be kept | You must keep the promise no matter what
